From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: IWMWriter header information and preprocessing

The writer did not answer IWMHeaderInfo, IWMHeaderInfo2, IWMHeaderInfo3 and
IWMWriterPreprocess (todo_wine in the conformance test, removed here).

- IWMHeaderInfo/2/3 on the writer share its reference count and keep what
  goes into the file header: attributes (typed and size-checked: WORD 2, DWORD
  and BOOL 4, QWORD 8, GUID 16 bytes, STRING of whole characters, BINARY any;
  names compared without regard to case; SetAttribute replaces the attribute
  of that name, AddAttribute adds one per language), markers and scripts
  (kept in time order), codec descriptions. The SDK's size protocol
  (ASF_E_BUFFERTOOSMALL with the size, NULL buffer for the size), ASF_E_NOTFOUND
  for an absent name, E_INVALIDARG for a bad index.
- IWMWriterPreprocess: the inputs listed for a profile never need preprocessing
  (GetMaxPreprocessingPasses is 0, SetNumPreprocessingPasses accepts only 0),
  so BeginPreprocessingPass, PreprocessSample and EndPreprocessingPass answer
  NS_E_INVALID_REQUEST after their argument checks (NS_E_INVALIDPROFILE without
  a profile, E_INVALIDARG for a bad input or flags).

---
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
index 88bc838..3f7e131 100644
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
@@ -11,4 +11,5 @@ SOURCES = \
 	profile_xml.c \
 	version.rc \
 	wmvcore_main.c \
-	writer.c
+	writer.c \
+	writer_header.c
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/profile.h b/dlls/wmvcore/profile.h
index f1736c3..3a27219 100644
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/profile.h
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/profile.h
@@ -41,4 +41,10 @@ void wm_free_media_type(WM_MEDIA_TYPE *mt);
 /* A memory buffer for samples (INSSBuffer) of the given capacity. */
 HRESULT wm_buffer_create(DWORD size, INSSBuffer **out);
 
+/* IWMHeaderInfo3 of the writer: attributes, markers, scripts and codec descriptions. */
+struct writer_header;
+HRESULT writer_header_create(IUnknown *outer, struct writer_header **out);
+IWMHeaderInfo3 *writer_header_iface(struct writer_header *header);
+void writer_header_destroy(struct writer_header *header);
+
 #endif
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/tests/wmvcore.c b/dlls/wmvcore/tests/wmvcore.c
index 516ee75..d8aac6c 100644
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/tests/wmvcore.c
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/tests/wmvcore.c
@@ -165,10 +165,10 @@ static void test_wmwriter_interfaces(void)
     check_interface(writer, &IID_IWMWriterAdvanced, TRUE);
